        "The southwest monsoon is moderate, but the northeast monsoon and cyclone remnants from October to December can bring heavy rain, cut roads and interrupt power. The Kattaleru bridge near Gampalagudem was washed away in floods in 2020, which shows what a bad season can do. Drafts and mock papers are best finished before this window, with a mobile hotspot ready.",
        "Sankranti in mid-January is the big family holiday; schools close for days and relatives travel. Ugadi, Vinayaka Chavithi, Dasara, Deepavali, Christmas and Ramzan reshape weekly routines too, and Dasara at Vijayawada draws crowds from across the district. The simple pattern is to fix a weekday evening and a weekend slot, then name the festival days that will be skipped.",
        "Exams overlay all this: IB May sessions with results in early July and November retakes, Cambridge in May-June and October-November, Edexcel in January and May-June. A student aiming at May should use the cooler months, November to February, for the heaviest teaching, and treat March and April as consolidation before the heat and the mango rush.",
