  faqs: [
    { question: "Can I find a school for IB or IGCSE in Tiruvuru itself?", answer: "Not one we could confirm, in the town or its revenue division. Schools here follow the Andhra Pradesh state board or CBSE. Directory listings show an IB school and a Cambridge IGCSE school in Vijayawada, and Hyderabad has more, but each should be verified with the school. Most families keep the current school and add an online tutor." },
    { question: "Do you send tutors to houses in Tiruvuru?", answer: "No. Home visits are offered only in Gurugram and parts of Delhi NCR, so nobody travels to Tiruvuru. Your child gets online home tuition instead: a live one-to-one lesson on a laptop, taken from home, with the tutor on video and a whiteboard both can write on. It is private teaching in every sense except physical presence." },
    { question: "We live near Tiruvuru. How do we get started?", answer: "Send us the programme or board, the subject and level, where your child stands now and the exam session in view. Because the district has no pool of IB teachers, we search across India for someone who has taught that course recently and propose one with a reason. A free trial lesson follows, and you decide after seeing the teaching." },
    { question: "What will an IB or IGCSE tutor cost us?", answer: "There is no rate card. Expect the figure to reflect the programme and level, the length and frequency of sessions, and how recently the tutor has taught your exact specification; it reaches you in writing before you book. Your location does not enter into it. With a free first lesson, you can judge the teaching before any money is discussed." },
    { question: "What is the free trial lesson like?", answer: "It is a normal lesson on a real topic from your child's syllabus, taught online by the tutor we propose. The tutor asks questions to find where understanding is firm or shaky and explains one or two ideas. Afterwards you get a plan for the first month and the written rate, and you can continue, adjust or ask for someone else." },
    { question: "Does the tutor write the IA, Extended Essay or coursework?", answer: "No. A tutor can explain what the criteria mean, help narrow a question, discuss how data might be gathered and comment frankly on a draft the student has written. Anything written or supplied for the student would violate IB academic-integrity rules and risk the qualification, so our tutors decline that work." },
    { question: "Our child is in Telugu-medium schooling. Will IB or IGCSE be too hard?", answer: "It is demanding but workable, provided the plan includes written English. Students from Telugu-medium classes often understand the science and maths well but have written few extended answers in English. Tutors build a glossary, teach command words and set a short weekly written answer, marked against the real scheme, so language and content grow together." },
    { question: "Which subjects can a tutor cover for an IB Diploma student?", answer: "Nearly every Diploma subject is possible: Maths AA and AI, Physics, Chemistry and Biology, then Economics, Business, Computer Science, Psychology, Geography, English A, Hindi B and TOK. Telugu A: Literature is checked when we read your brief. Tell us the subject, HL or SL and the session you are targeting, and we will say plainly whether a suitable specialist is free." },
    { question: "Can younger children in Tiruvuru get IB PYP or MYP help?", answer: "Yes. For PYP, lessons build reading, writing and number sense alongside the research habits the Exhibition rewards, in short, regular sessions. For MYP, they cover criterion-based tasks in sciences, maths and language, plus the Personal Project journal. With no IB school nearby, a tutor can preserve routines that a child who transfers would otherwise drop." },
    { question: "IGCSE without an IGCSE school: how do private candidates sit the exams?", answer: "By entering through an authorised exam centre, which handles registration and any practical or speaking component. Decide on Cambridge or Pearson Edexcel, fix the syllabus code and tier, then ask a centre, probably in Vijayawada or Hyderabad, whether private candidates are welcome and what the cut-off date is. Ask early; places and deadlines shift." },
    { question: "Which IGCSE board suits us better, Cambridge or Pearson Edexcel?", answer: "Whichever has an accessible centre, dates and a subject list that fit your household; both are recognised worldwide. Cambridge sits in May-June and October-November, Edexcel in January and May-June. Once you choose, keep all past papers and mark schemes from that board, because the two phrase questions differently." },
    { question: "How do we cope with power cuts, heat and cyclone-season rain?", answer: "Tell the tutor as soon as a lesson is affected and reconnect when supply returns; a phone hotspot is a good backup. A lost half hour can normally be recovered by moving another session that week. Heat suggests early or late slots, and rain suggests finishing drafts and mock papers a few days before any deadline." },
    { question: "Can lessons work around the mango season and Sankranti?", answer: "Yes. Most families choose one weekday evening and one weekend slot, then tell the tutor which festival or harvest-rush days to drop or shift. An extra session before a mock or an exam series is simple to add online, since no one has to travel to make up time." },
    { question: "When is the ideal time to begin?", answer: "As close to the first day of the course as you can manage: Class 11 for the IB Diploma, Grade 9 for IGCSE. That leaves time to fix written English, learn what each command word wants and sketch the first Internal Assessment before deadlines bite. Joining later is still worthwhile; the tutor then picks the topics worth most marks and leans on timed papers before the next series." },
    { question: "What about AP EAPCET, NEET and JEE if my child takes IB or IGCSE?", answer: "Quite a few families want the state entrance routes kept open, and that can work if the timetable is realistic. The subject content overlaps but the question styles do not, so entrance practice and IB or IGCSE practice need separate slots. Our tutors handle only the IB or IGCSE teaching. Before choosing both, read the eligibility notes for your board in each exam's latest bulletin." },
    { question: "How will universities view an IB or IGCSE record?", answer: "Indian universities generally accept it once the Association of Indian Universities issues equivalence, CUET-UG is open to every board, and EAPCET, NEET and JEE each set their own conditions for other-board candidates. Overseas, predicted grades drive offers. Start equivalence paperwork early in Class 12 and confirm each institution's rules directly." },
    { question: "What if the tutor does not suit?", answer: "Say so and we will propose someone else. Progress is checked every few weeks, and swapping tutors is a normal part of how this service works rather than a complaint. The free first lesson is there to show up a poor match early, and because the rate is agreed in writing at the outset, a swap causes no surprises." },
    { question: "Is IB Gram part of any school, exam board or university?", answer: "No. IB Gram is run on its own, with no tie to the IB, Cambridge, Pearson or any school, college or university mentioned here, and it cannot speak on their behalf. Their names are included only to show which options exist around Tiruvuru. Whether a student is admitted, entered for an exam or granted equivalence is for those organisations to decide." },
  ],

